    STEP A-3.20: Restore Normal Realloc Failure Coverage + TSan Direct Hook
    
    Resolves A-3.19 audit finding: T10 was rewritten to test bootstrap realloc
    (A-3.19), which lost the normal realloc failure coverage from A-3.18.
    
    Changes:
      T10 (bootstrap realloc): KEPT unchanged from A-3.19
      T11 (NEW): Normal realloc failure injection — restored from A-3.18 design
        - Uses profiler interposition (malloc/realloc wrappers)
        - Injects failure into real_realloc via __profiler_v6_test_set_real_realloc
        - Verifies: ptr valid, tracking intact (F3), data intact, retry succeeds
        - Runs in Plain Suite; SKIPPED under TSan (requires interposition)
      T12 (NEW): Normal realloc tracking via direct hook — TSan coverage
        - Uses __profiler_v6_test_normal_realloc_tracked (new hook)
        - Exercises track_free/track_alloc code paths directly (no interposition)
        - Tests: success (track_free old, track_alloc new), failure (preserved),
          retry after failure
        - Runs under TSan (no SKIP_IF_DISABLED)
    
    New profiler hooks:
      __profiler_v6_test_set_real_realloc() — for failure injection
      __profiler_v6_test_get_real_realloc() — save/restore real_realloc
      __profiler_v6_test_normal_realloc_tracked() — exercises normal realloc
        tracking logic directly (track_free on success, track_alloc on new,
        preserve on failure)
    
    Results:
      Plain suite: 121 tests, exit 0 (T1-T12 all pass)
      TSan: exit 0, 0 data races, 0 size aborts
        T8:  RAN (not skipped)
        T9:  RAN (not skipped)
        T10: RAN (not skipped) — bootstrap realloc
        T11: SKIPPED (expected — requires interposition)
        T12: RAN (not skipped) — normal realloc tracking direct
      Node smoke: exit 0
      PROD isolation: verified (nm -D, zero test-hook symbols)
    
    Coverage matrix:
      Bootstrap realloc: T10 (plain + TSan via direct hooks)
      Normal realloc failure: T11 (plain only) + T12 (TSan via direct hook)
      Both paths covered, no regression from A-3.18.
    
    No push to feature branch (awaiting Steward approval).

